// BT-3556 (ADR 0124 Section 8/B9) regression fixture: an *untyped* Actor
// with a `late` slot — `late` needs no `typed` class to be legal, only a
// type annotation on the slot itself (docs/beamtalk-language-features.md's
// `late` Slots section). Paired with typed_late_slot_actor.bt to pin that
// "absent + late stays absent" holds on both a typed and an untyped class,
// not just the typed one the old typed-no-default failure already covered.

Actor subclass: UntypedLateSlotActor
  late state: proc :: String
  state: label :: String = "unset"

  getLabel => ^self.label
